Myshell - PART 1

About - 

    This programs implements PART 1 of a simplified shell. It read the commands inputed by the user,
parse into individual tokens using the strtok(), check for special characters as "<,>,&" and handle them.
After that it stores inside an Param object.

How to Compile Using Makefile -

    To compile and be able to use the program you should use the command:
        make
    It will generate the executable file.
    
    To cleanup and remove the compiled program use:
        make clean
    It will cleanup the executable file.

How to Use the Program -

    Run the myshell normally with:
        ./myshell
    It will start the program normally without the Debug mode

    Run the myshell in debug mode with: 
        ./myshell -Debug
    It will start the progam with debug mode activated. When it is activated
    it will print the contents stored in the param object.

    The myshell program will automatically display:
        $$$
    Meaning the program is working correctly.

    Type and enter "exit" to terminate the program.